Source: jvc
Section: devel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: mplx <jennifer@mplx.dev>
Homepage: https://github.com/jennifer-language/jvc
Vcs-Browser: https://github.com/jennifer-language/jvc
Vcs-Git: https://github.com/jennifer-language/jvc.git
Standards-Version: 4.6.2

Package: jvc
Architecture: all
Depends: jennifer (>= @ENGINE_FLOOR@)
Recommends: git
Description: deck manager for the Jennifer programming language
 jvc resolves, vendors and publishes Jennifer decks, as composer does for
 PHP or cargo for Rust. It reads a deck.toml, resolves the dependency graph
 against a deck repository, and pins the result in camcorder.lock, so a
 fresh checkout plus `jvc install` reproduces the same code.
 .
 The package is architecture-independent Jennifer source: the launcher at
 /usr/bin/jvc is a symlink into /usr/share/jvc, where bin/ and src/ sit
 side by side because the launcher reaches its modules through a relative
 import.
 .
 The versioned dependency on jennifer mirrors the [engines] table in jvc's
 deck.toml; the interpreter enforces the same floor at load time from each
 source file's `# pragma-jennifer-version:` header.
 .
 git is recommended, not required: installing tar.gz decks from a
 repository uses HTTP only. git is needed for [sources] decks, registry
 decks of kind git, `jvc app install`, and publishing.
